                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A follower of John Duns Scotus, Franciscan scholar, who maintained certain doctrines in philosophy and theology in opposition to the Thomists."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aaae1069-b135-43d5-9211-25bbda20d62e",
                                                "sense_id": "62cc1227-be53-3b2f-b633-7fbfda5a48d4",
                                                "text": "[…] it should be remembered that their poets and rabbis of the middle ages were contemporary with the Scotists and Thomists, with the pseudo-platonism and peripateticism of Christendom."
